## Subject

Write `<kind>(<scope>)?!?: <description>` once. Kind is one of
`feat|fix|docs|refactor|test|style|perf|build|ci|chore`; use `chore` only for repo maintenance,
tooling, config, or dependencies. Scope is optional; when absent, omit it and its parentheses. A scope uses only
lowercase letters, digits, `/`, `_`, or `-`: no dots, no uppercase. Use one space after the colon and
a lowercase imperative description. Keep the frontmatter value unquoted. Write the first valid subject;
do not generate alternatives. There is no length limit.

## Body

Omit the body only for a one-line typo, formatting, or comment change; every other commit gets a body. Otherwise
explain why in one `## Body` item. Use `## Body Summary`, `## Body Details`, and
`## Body Footer` instead only for migration steps, breaking changes, or issue
references.

## Document shape

For a commit, use frontmatter `type: commit` and `subject:`, then the selected
body form. Optional `## Files` lists paths; optional `## Excluded Files` uses
`path | reason`, where valid reasons are internal_ignore, not_task_related, sensitive, deferred.
When no commit is needed, submit only `type: skip`
and `reason:` frontmatter.

